.\" -*- nroff -*-
.TH ucc 1 2002-03-24 Exult

.SH NAME
ucc \- UseCode Compiler for Exult

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ucc
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ FILE ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Games supported by Exult (\fIUltima VII\fR, for example) consist in
large part of Usecode.
.BR exult (1)
basically implements a virtual machine the machine language of which
is Usecode.

.B ucc
is a compiler that targets this machine language.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
Display detailed help, including all warning categories, defaults, and examples,
then exit successfully without compiling or writing output.
.TP
.BI \-o " FILE"
Write bytecode to FILE. Compilation errors preserve any previous output.
Without this option, the input extension is replaced by .uco (or .uco is
appended if there is no extension). Standard input defaults to a.ucout.
.TP
.BI \-I " DIRECTORY"
Add an include search directory. May be repeated.
The UCC_INCLUDE environment variable adds one further include directory.
.TP
.B \-s
Select Serpent Isle intrinsics unless overridden by a #game directive.
.TP
.B \-b
Omit the symbol table.
.TP
.BI \-c " MODE"
Use colored diagnostics always, never, or auto (the default).
.TP
.BI \-W NAME
Enable a warning category. Use \-Wno\-NAME to disable it.
Categories are goto, integer\-coercion, shape\-to\-function,
constant\-condition, unreachable\-code, implicit\-return\-type,
implicit\-function\-kind, autonumber, missing\-game, missing\-itemref,
constructor\-arguments, unknown\-directives, unknown\-escape\-sequence,
function\-id\-alias, and general.
All categories except function\-id\-alias are enabled by default.
The function\-id\-alias category warns about compatible declarations that
give different names to the same explicit function ID. Both names remain
usable. Incompatible declarations and multiple definitions remain errors.
.TP
.B \-Wall, \-Wno\-all
Enable or disable all warning categories.
.TP
.B \-Werror, \-Wno\-error
Treat enabled warnings as errors, or restore ordinary warning severity.
Use \-Werror=NAME to enable and promote an individual category, and
\-Wno\-error=NAME to exempt it from promotion.
.TP
.B \-u
Disable all warning categories. Hard errors remain enabled.
.TP
.B \-\-
End options, allowing an input filename beginning with a hyphen.

.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Diagnostics are written to standard error and include the source filename,
line, byte column, and a source excerpt when available. Warning messages
identify their controlling \-W option. Standard output contains compilation
status messages. The exit status is zero on success and nonzero on failure.
If FILE is omitted, source is read from standard input.
Command-line option and argument errors suggest using \-h for help.

